	When to use Factory Methods
	
	Factory methods are great when:
	You want to encapsulate object creation logic.
	You don’t want calling code to know the concrete implementation.
	You want flexibility to change implementations without changing the client code.
	
	Example Use Cases:
	Payment processing: PaymentFactory.getPayment("CreditCard") returns a CreditCardPayment object.
	Document generation: DocumentFactory.getDocument("PDF") returns a PDF document.
	Notification system: NotificationFactory.getNotification("Email") returns an email notification.